<MudContainer MaxWidth="MaxWidth.Small">
    <MudText Typo="Typo.overline" HtmlTag="p">Observatory notes · 3 min read</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.h5" HtmlTag="h3" GutterBottom="true">Why the dome stays cold</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-3">
        A telescope sees best when its mirror matches the night air. Warm glass bends the light above it into shimmering
        currents, and stars that should be points swell into soft discs.
    </MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
        So the dome opens an hour before the first visitors arrive, and the heaters stay off. Bring a coat: the
        sharpest views of the evening come after the mirror has given up the last of the day's warmth.
    </MudText>
</MudContainer>
